                  %a{:href => "https://books.google.de/books/about/Applied_Exterior_Calculus.html?id=GUkViODKZ2oC"} GoogleBooks
          %p
            With an eye towards application in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikio+Nakahara"}> Mikio Nakahara
              , Chapter 6 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometry%2C+Topology+and+Physics"} Geometry, Topology and Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781315275826"} doi:10.1201/9781315275826
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://alpha.sinp.msu.ru/~panov/LibBooks/GRAV/(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)Mikio_Nakahara-Geometry,_Topology_and_Physics,_Second_Edition_(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)-Institute_of_Physics_Publishing(2003).pdf"} pdf
          %h3#in_algebraic_geometry In algebraic geometry
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p A useful introduction is
          %ul
            %li
              Kiran Kedlaya,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-adic cohomology, from theory to practice
              (
              %a{:href => "http://swc.math.arizona.edu/aws/2007/KedlayaNotes11Mar.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A classical reference on the algebraic version is
          %ul#Grothendieck
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the De Rham cohomology of algebraic varieties
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 29
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=PMIHES_1966__29__95_0"} numdam
          %ul
            %li
              A. Grothendieck,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Crystals and the de Rham cohomology of schemes
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 3
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=0269663"} MR0269663
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~leila/grothendieckcircle/DixExp.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robin+Hartshorne"}> Robin Hartshorne
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the de Rham cohomology of algebraic varieties
              %strong 45
              (1975), p. 5-99
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=55:5633"} MR55#5633
            %li
              P. Monsky,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Finiteness of de Rham cohomology
              %strong 94
              (1972), 237–245,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=301017"} MR301017
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.2307/2373603"} doi
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Yves André,
                %em Comparison theorems between algebraic and analytic De Rham cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/journals/JTNB/2004-2/pages335-355.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em DG-Modules over the de Rham complex and the vanishing cycles functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1479
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0086264"} doi:10.1007/BFb0086264
